# generated datasets over GitHub's 100 MB hard limit
#
# Each is committed as its .tar.xz sibling instead — 600.8 MB -> 34.1 MB for the
# corpus — so the data is still in the repo, just not as raw JSON. Regenerate
# with `tar -xJf <name>.tar.xz`, or rebuild from scratch (the corpus takes hours
# of NCBI calls, so prefer the archive).
#
# Sizes at time of writing: 600.8 MB, 255.7 MB, 193.5 MB.
datasets/oa_corpus_full.json
datasets/oa_corpus_full.v1.json
datasets/dataset2/records2.json

# Rust build artifacts
#
# `rust/target` reached 736 MB across 1,503 files and was once committed whole;
# every one of them is reproducible from `cargo build`.
rust/target/

# Reconstruction runs written by main.rs. Small per run and worth keeping for
# comparison, so this ignores nothing by default — but a full-corpus export is
# 102,240 records and belongs in the datasets convention (.tar.xz), not here.
# rust/runs/
